-- Tests for wra3-sch12.l4 (Schedule 12). Expected values are written from the text (raw lines 3497-3527), decided before running.

§ `sch 12 definitions`

#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body is an appeal tribunal` `sch 12 an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body is an appeal tribunal` `sch 12 a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 to the Social Security Act 1998` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body is an appeal tribunal` `sch 12 any other body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body is a Child Support Commissioner` `sch 12 a person appointed as a Child Support Commissioner under section 22 of the Child Support Act 1991` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body is a Child Support Commissioner` `sch 12 a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 to the Social Security Act 1998` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body is a Child Support Commissioner` `sch 12 any other body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 4(3) SSA1998 10(7) the body is a Commissioner` `sch 12 a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 to the Social Security Act 1998` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 4(3) SSA1998 10(7) the body is a Commissioner` `sch 12 a tribunal of persons appointed as Social Security Commissioners` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 4(3) SSA1998 10(7) the body is a Commissioner` `sch 12 any other body` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body whose functions have been transferred is now` `sch 12 an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998` EQUALS JUST `the First-tier Tribunal`
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body whose functions have been transferred is now` `sch 12 a person appointed as a Child Support Commissioner under section 22 of the Child Support Act 1991` EQUALS JUST `the Upper Tribunal`
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body whose functions have been transferred is now` `sch 12 a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 to the Social Security Act 1998` EQUALS JUST `the Upper Tribunal`
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body whose functions have been transferred is now` `sch 12 a tribunal of persons appointed as Social Security Commissioners` EQUALS JUST `the Upper Tribunal`
#ASSERT `sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body whose functions have been transferred is now` `sch 12 any other body` EQUALS NOTHING

